#====================================================================
# DRAFT-mysqltuner-shadow-ci-readonly-tmp - manual shadow CI on OHOS can fail silently when /tmp is read-only
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-mysqltuner-shadow-ci-readonly-tmp
trigger_tool:           ssh|zsh|ci/conan/build_and_test.sh|mktemp
phase:                  shadow_ci|l0_preflight
error_signature:        L0: Quality gate checks\.\.\.$|mktemp: Failed to create file /tmp/.*Read-only file system|can't create temporary file /tmp/
severity:               2
category:               ohos|shadow-ci|tmp|runner
match_keywords:         mysqltuner, shadow CI, /tmp, TMPDIR, TMPPREFIX, mktemp, zsh here-doc, read-only file system, L0 silent exit
title:                  Set TMPPREFIX and wrap mktemp to job-local tmp when manual OHOS shadow CI has read-only /tmp
topic: >
  mysqltuner/2.9.1 manual shadow CI exited after the L0 banner with no detail.
  Direct probes showed /tmp was read-only and mktemp ignored TMPDIR unless -p
  was supplied.
root_cause: >
  CI L0 uses mktemp and here-docs. On the device, /tmp is read-only; system
  mktemp defaults to /tmp and zsh here-doc temp files also need TMPPREFIX.
durable_solution: >
  For manual isolated runs, export TMPDIR to the job-local writable tmp,
  export TMPPREFIX="$TMPDIR/zsh", and invoke setup/build through a zsh wrapper
  that defines mktemp() as "command mktemp -p \"$TMPDIR\" \"$@\"".
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           shadow-ci-job-local-temp
rec_command:            export TMPDIR="$JOB/tmp" TMPPREFIX="$TMPDIR/zsh"; zsh -c 'mktemp() { command mktemp -p "$TMPDIR" "$@"; }; . ./ci/conan/build_and_test.sh'
rec_auto_fix:           false
verification_cmd:       mktemp -p "$TMPDIR" && CI_PACKAGES="archives/m/mysqltuner/2.9.1" zsh ci/conan/build_and_test.sh
evidence_chain: >
  mysqltuner/2.9.1 first run stopped at L0; after TMPPREFIX plus mktemp wrapper,
  L0 printed all checks and final shadow CI exited 0.
limitations: >
  This is a manual shadow-CI invocation workaround. Package PRs should not
  change shared CI infrastructure for a single package.
doc_file:               archives/m/mysqltuner/2.9.1/knowledge_drafts/DRAFT-mysqltuner-shadow-ci-readonly-tmp.md
last_updated:           2026-09-11
source_event:           mysqltuner 2.9.1 manual isolated OHOS shadow CI
metrics_success_count:  1
metrics_fail_count:     0
metrics_confidence:     0.85
draft:                  true
